# Sources of the host-language-grammars study (hub 3.11). Old-body files were read at commit b8ff978c9; files removed by the cut of 2026-09-29 were read from the tree one commit before 115fea55e. Line ranges sit in the citing claim.

n: 2.19
name: host-language-grammars-sources
kind: hub
is: The primary sources behind hub 3.11: the study report on the old body's host-language grammars; the five host-language rule files, the two rule engines and the files around them at commit b8ff978c9; six files the cut of 2026-09-29 removed, read from the tree one commit before it; two NUMS.Go configuration files; two first-round reports on NUMS.Go; and four web pages on grammars that both parse and print.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 2.19.1
name: gap-host-language-grammars.md
kind: source
is: The study report of round 2 on gap G4, 643 lines: what the five host-language rule files read and write back, how a rule is held as data, whether two languages reach one node, the cost per language, and a C probe of one rule set that reads and prints.
path: coherence-seed/study/r2/gap-host-language-grammars.md
date: 2026-11-24
got: 2026-11-24
at: 2026-11-24

